You know, I went to the bakery at the station.
The bakeries in the station are open on Sunday too.
I bought a Brötchen there for my breakfast.
That cost two euros.
I put it in my backpack.
Then I walked up the stairs to the platform.
I arrived at the top exactly on time.
My S-Bahn to Potsdam just pulled in.
So I boarded quickly.
On the train I looked for a seat.
I walked through the carriage.
Luckily I found a great seat by the window.
I sat down and opened my backpack.
Then I ate my Brötchen.
The train departed.
I looked out of the window contentedly.
